  "name": "BETA HCG (CSF)",
  "code": "1741",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"51\" data-end=\"94\">Beta-hCG (human chorionic gonadotropin)</strong> test in <strong data-start=\"103\" data-end=\"132\">cerebrospinal fluid (CSF)</strong> is a specialized investigation primarily used in the evaluation of <strong data-start=\"200\" data-end=\"233\">intracranial germ cell tumors</strong>, especially <strong data-start=\"246\" data-end=\"259\">germinoma</strong> and <strong data-start=\"264\" data-end=\"283\">choriocarcinoma</strong>, which may occur in the <strong data-start=\"308\" data-end=\"332\">brain or spinal cord</strong>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Beta-hCG in CSF</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Undetectable / Very Low (&lt;5 IU/L)</strong></td>\n<td>Normal &ndash; no evidence of hCG-secreting tumor in CNS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Elevated (&gt;5 IU/L)</strong></td>\n<td>Suggestive of <strong>CNS germ cell tumor</strong> (e.g., choriocarcinoma, germinoma); must be interpreted with clinical and imaging findings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Markedly Elevated (&gt;50&ndash;100 IU/L)</strong></td>\n<td>Strongly suggestive of <strong>choriocarcinoma</strong> or <strong>mixed germ cell tumor</strong> with choriocarcinoma components</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1287\" data-end=\"1311\"><strong data-start=\"1291\" data-end=\"1311\">Supporting Tests</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1312\" data-end=\"1606\">\n<li data-start=\"1312\" data-end=\"1516\">\n<p data-start=\"1314\" data-end=\"1407\"><strong data-start=\"1314\" data-end=\"1332\">Serum beta-hCG</strong> should be measured <strong data-start=\"1352\" data-end=\"1369\">alongside CSF</strong> to calculate the <strong data-start=\"1387\" data-end=\"1406\">CSF:serum ratio</strong>.</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1410\" data-end=\"1516\">\n<li data-start=\"1410\" data-end=\"1516\">\n<p data-start=\"1412\" data-end=\"1516\">A <strong data-start=\"1414\" data-end=\"1445\">CSF:serum beta-hCG ratio &gt;1</strong> or <strong data-start=\"1449\" data-end=\"1493\">disproportionately elevated CSF beta-hCG</strong> supports a CNS origin.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1517\" data-end=\"1606\">\n<p data-start=\"1519\" data-end=\"1606\"><strong data-start=\"1519\" data-end=\"1550\">CSF alpha-fetoprotein (AFP)</strong> may also be done to help classify CNS germ cell tumors.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1613\" data-end=\"1669\"><strong data-start=\"1617\" data-end=\"1669\">Conditions Associated with Elevated CSF Beta-hCG</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1838\">\n<li data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1723\">\n<p data-start=\"1672\" data-end=\"1723\"><strong data-start=\"1672\" data-end=\"1723\">Germinoma (with syncytiotrophoblastic elements)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1724\" data-end=\"1745\">\n<p data-start=\"1726\" data-end=\"1745\"><strong data-start=\"1726\" data-end=\"1745\">Choriocarcinoma</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1746\" data-end=\"1771\">\n<p data-start=\"1748\" data-end=\"1771\"><strong data-start=\"1748\" data-end=\"1771\">Embryonal carcinoma</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1772\" data-end=\"1838\">\n<p data-start=\"1774\" data-end=\"1838\">Rarely, <strong data-start=\"1782\" data-end=\"1831\">metastatic testicular or trophoblastic tumors</strong> to CNS</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1845\" data-end=\"1864\"><strong data-start=\"1849\" data-end=\"1864\">Limitations</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1865\" data-end=\"2048\">\n<li data-start=\"1865\" data-end=\"1965\">\n<p data-start=\"1867\" data-end=\"1965\">Cannot distinguish between different types of germ cell tumors without imaging and histopathology.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1966\" data-end=\"2048\">\n<p data-start=\"1968\" data-end=\"2048\">False positives are rare but may occur due to contamination or technical issues.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
